WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
Three doors.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.710
The first says: the law.

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.710
The second: charity.

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.720
The third: me.

5
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.450
A man in a top hat walks
straight past all three.

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.210
Above him, the year ticks up to 1843.

7
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.800
Two gentlemen ask him to give to the poor.

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.870
His reply?

9
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:19.890
"Nothing!"

10
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.660
So whose business is it?

11
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.690
Which of those doors
should open for the poor?

12
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.510
In this mission, you'll hear Scrooge
turn the charity collectors away,

13
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.160
line by line.

14
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:35.510
You'll go back to 1798, when Thomas
Malthus argued that population grows faster

15
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.680
than food.

16
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:42.180
And to February 1843, when a report
described children's working lives.

17
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: decide who
should help the poor.
